# <%= book_title %>

An interactive EPUB 3 book made with [bkr](https://github.com/sophiedeziel/bkr).

## Writing

- **Metadata and chapter order** live in `config/book.yml` (title, author, language, chapters, ...).
- **Chapters** are HTML files in `content/`. Each one is a body fragment: no `<html>`, `<head>`
  or `<body>`, just your content, starting with an `<h1>`. It must be well-formed XHTML: close
  every tag, write `<br/>` and `<img ... />`, and escape `&` as `&amp;`.
- **Styles** go in `assets/css/`, **scripts** in `assets/js/`, **images** in `assets/images/` and
  **fonts** in `assets/fonts/`. Everything in `assets/` is packaged into the EPUB.
- **Images in chapters**: reference them relative to the chapter file, e.g.
  `<img src="../assets/images/photo.png" alt="..." />`. Links between chapters work too:
  `<a href="02_interactive.html">`. bkr rewrites both to the right paths inside the EPUB.
- bkr ships `bkr.css` and `bkr.js`, which give you nice typography and interactive widgets
  (reveal boxes, quizzes, ...). See `content/02_interactive.html` for examples. Turn them off
  with `bkr_assets: false` in `config/book.yml`.

## Building

```sh
book build      # creates build/<name>.epub
book validate   # checks the EPUB with the W3C EPUBCheck (needs Java)
```

Open the `.epub` in any EPUB 3 reader (Apple Books, Thorium, Calibre, ...).
